  "name": "Anycubic Kobra 2 series toolhead (Kobra 2 / 2 Pro / 2 Plus / 2 Max / 2 Neo)",
  "provenance": "Anycubic Kobra 2 series toolhead (Kobra 2 / 2 Pro / 2 Plus / 2 Max / 2 Neo) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1699568 (Kobra 2 Series Hotend Assembly CAD, reverse engineered STEP: nozzle, heater block, heatbreak, heatsink); https://www.printables.com/model/917189 (Spare Kobra 2 Hotend Housing & Fanduct, re-engineered stock front housing 74x73x98 mm and stock-fit duct); https://www.printables.com/model/724096 (Mantis quick-release duct, uses stock 5020 blower); https://www.printables.com/model/699890 (blower quick-release bracket, replaces stock cover); https://store.anycubic.com/products/hotend-module (printhead assembly photos S010132 Kobra 2 Pro/Plus/Max, S010077 Kobra 2 Neo); https://store.anycubic.com/products/hotend-for-fdm-3d-printers (Kobra 2 heating block assembly photo S010107); https://store.anycubic.com/products/cooling-fan (Kobra 2 series: 3010 hotend fan, 5020 dual-intake model blower); https://store.anycubic.com/products/heater (Kobra 2 series heater cartridge 6x19 mm, vertical). Frame: nozzle tip at origin, +Y toward printer back. Nozzle/heater-block geometry measured from the reverse-engineered Kobra 2 Series hotend STEP (printables 1699568; parts named 'Kobra 2 Neo', and the listing says the same hotend is shared by the whole Kobra 2 line, which Anycubic's store confirms with one heating block assembly for Kobra 2/Pro/Plus/Max/Neo). Nozzle: tip flat r0.5, cone to r2.0 at z1.75 (about 41 deg half-angle), hex 7.6 mm across flats to z5.25, block underside at z6.05; the stock silicone sock (store photo S010107) puts the lowest non-nozzle surface about z4.8, and 4.5 is used. Housing size from the re-engineered stock housing STL (printables 917189): 74 W x 98 H, front wall plus side walls running about 72 mm deep, flat underside. Store photo S010132 (Kobra 2 Pro) shows the finned duct face and the housing bottom level with the sock bottom and the brass nozzle just below, so duct and housing are placed at z5.0 (about 0.5 above the sock), conservatively spread over the full housing footprint. Nozzle is centred in X; in Y it is placed 40 mm behind the housing front face (blower and 23 mm-deep duct plenum in front, duct legs alongside the block), which leaves about 32 mm of housing behind it. Kobra 2 Neo: same hotend, but the housing is the chevron-vent Kobra Neo-style shroud (store photo S010077) with a narrower V-faceted bottom and the blower inside. From the photo its underside is about 5-6 mm above the tip, so the same levels cover it conservatively. Gantry (X extrusion on V-wheels behind the carriage plate): z35 and y33..58 are estimated from the head proportions; no CAD was available. [1] Footnote: duct, housing and gantry heights are photo/derived estimates (about +-1 mm); the hotend is from a community reverse-engineered model, not Anycubic CAD. parts: per-component boxes with no 0.3 margin. Estimated/derived parts are extended about 0.2-0.5 mm outward and downward for uncertainty. Mid-frame-to-tip offset: housing front face at y=-40.5, housing bottom about z4.8-5.0. Nozzle: land radius 0.50 mm, 41.4-degree cone to Z=1.75, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 35.00 mm above the tip, Y 33.0..58.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/anycubic-kobra2.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
